---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { me } from '../../../data.js';

const title = 'GrammarLens support';
const description = 'How to get help with GrammarLens, report a bug, or ask a question.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Support</strong>
      One developer<br />
      Replies within<br />
      a few days
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h1 class="display">Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        GrammarLens is made by one person. Email me and you'll reach me directly, not a ticket
        queue.
      </p>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>
          <span class="links-label">Email</span>
          <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Bug reports</strong>
      What to include so<br />
      I can actually fix it
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>Send an email with as much of this as you have:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>What you were doing when it happened</li>
        <li>What you expected, and what happened instead</li>
        <li>Your iPhone model and iOS version</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if the problem is visible</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I read everything that comes in. I can't promise a fix for every request, but I will tell you
        whether it's something I plan to change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Common questions</strong>
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h3>Does GrammarLens work offline?</h3>
      <p>
        No. Explanations are generated by a language model over the internet, so the app needs a
        connection to check a sentence.
      </p>

      <h3>Where is my practice history stored?</h3>
      <p>
        On your device. It isn't uploaded anywhere I can read.
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/privacy">More detail in the privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
      <p>
        Delete the app. Your practice history goes with it, because it never lived anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h3>Will there be an Android version?</h3>
      <p>
        The app is built in Flutter, so an Android build is technically possible. I haven't
        committed to one yet.
      </p>

      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Add later:</strong> replace these with the questions people actually ask once the
          app is out. Invented FAQs are filler; real ones are useful.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>More</strong>
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <ul class="links">
        <li>
          <span class="links-label">Product</span>
          <a href="/products/grammarlens">GrammarLens</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="links-label">Privacy</span>
          <a href="/products/grammarlens/privacy">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
